Welcome to Vanilla!

-------------------------------------------------
#### HUB

### 1. Introduction

VN (Vanilla) - it is a RISC-like ISA designed from the ground up.
Target: clear architecture with no legacy.


### 2. Main features
|
| bits              : 64
| registers         : 32     (x0-x31)
| hardwired reg     : x31    (control register, not general-purpose)
| instruction width : 64-bit (fixed)
| privileges        : hypervisor / kernel / user
| interrupts        : vectors, 256


### 2. Registers
|
| x0-x30        : general purpose
| x31           : hardwired, using for control features
| ... (about: MEMORY/Register File)

### 3. Memory
|
| reg. file     : register file, contains all general-purpose and hardwired registers
| MMIO          : memory-mapped I/O, base address and control flags in x31
| L1 cache      : fast memory only for cpu
| ... (about: MEMORY/)

### 4. Interrupts
|
| vector table  : used to describe handler addresses
| handlers      : handlers of cpu/peripheral devices
| ... (about: CORE/Interrupts)


